      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Contrary to your assumption, being transparent about the sensor data actually **de-escalates** the situation and prevents claims from escalating to a formal chargeback. If you lie about the cause (claiming it was \"damaged in transit\" when it likely wasn't), the customer will easily discover the discrepancy after the replacement is inspected, leading to renewed distrust and wasted administrative effort.\nThe most efficient strategy is to present the data as objective proof that the damage occurred after delivery (e.g., during unpacking), which legally absolves you of liability while still satisfying the customer with a replacement at no extra charge. This approach validates their experience without incurring false claim liability, ensuring you avoid the high cost and reputation damage of a successful chargeback attempt.",
